  "copy": {
    "series_title": "The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026",
    "caption": "The people behind Kraft Bräu are good friends, and they’re also the hosts of the festival that brings this series together. I’m delighted to feature the brewery’s beginnings in The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026.\n\nOn 28 September 1998, Kraft Bräu officially opened at Blesius Garten in Trier-Olewig. Hans-Werner Kraft and Klaus Tonkaboni established the house brewery, which launched with three unfiltered beers: a pale beer, a dark beer, and a wheat beer.\n\nJoin @kraft_braeu_trier and @blesius_garten for the Trier Beer Festival on 2–3 October 2026 at Blesius Garten, Trier.\n\nExplore “Kraft Bräu Opens in Trier” on Beer Chronicles through the link in the accompanying Story.\n\nTickets are still available:\nhttps://www.ticket-regional.de/events_info.php?eventID=275224\n\n#BeerChronicles #TrierBeerFestival #KraftBräu #Trier #BeerHistory",
    "story_text": "BEER CHRONICLES\nThe Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026\nKraft Bräu\n\n1998\nKraft Bräu opens in Trier.\n\nTRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN\nTickets still available — see feed caption\nbeer-chronicles.org\n\nNative link sticker: Explore their story\nhttps://beer-chronicles.org/?string=Kraft+Br%C3%A4u\n\nThis is an accessible transcript of the single Story. Add only the native link sticker to the artwork; do not duplicate this transcript as an overlay. Ticket details are in the feed post’s caption.",
    "alt_text": "Cream background with dark serif lettering and fine copper rules. At the top: “BEER CHRONICLES” and “The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026.” The original Kraft Bräu logo shows green lettering on a black square: “Kraft” in ornate letters above the spaced word “BRÄU.” Below it: “1998” and “Kraft Bräu opens in Trier.” The footer reads “TRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN,” followed by “beer-chronicles.org.”",
    "approval_status": "approved"
  },
